<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>concerning the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κουρῆτες, τὰ</span> K. treatises on the
			K., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.3.7
			</span></i>: hence, in Neo-Platonic theology, <i>ministrant</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ πρῶτος πατὴρ καὶ ὁ τρίτος οὐ
					παράγει κ. τάξιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					278
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. θεότης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procl.
					<u>in Ti.</u>
					3.310
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τάξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Theol.Plat.</u>
					5.35
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τριάς</span> ibid. (here
			derived fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κούρη</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κόρη</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			ὁ K. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῦς</span>) <i>the Cretic</i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				651
			</span></i>; <i>the third paeon</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υυ-υ</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Heph.</u>
				p.218C.
			</span></i></div>
